{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head c1452fd1ae9b02f367e5bf42e417a11dc7b559ad (tree df2b7db700fce7742618dc07a201880f6132e6f2), the notes-only continuation of a779ade8 on published main 8a9f9d1e. It carries three items: XD-1 (draft revision fence), Counting (finite fulfillment pairs) and the Security cleanup. Each item has its own conclusions below. The verdict binds the three implementation promises 2f7f1ef2 (XD-1), 4c2560ee (Counting) and fce117c4 (Security cleanup), with reporting artifacts de4ea736, 4e27e4c4 and c8a49454, and signs all 15 path artifacts. It replaces my unsigned review of a779ade8 under b4ce2c41, which `gs review` could not bind.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Artifacts.** The 15 filed artifacts equal the 15 changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only 8a9f9d1e c1452fd1`): none missing, none extra, none twice. Each rests only on its lane promise and the two gate ENDs, and `gs review --prepare` binds all three lanes.\n- **Source identity.** c1452fd1 differs from a779ade8 in three paths, all under `notes/` (`git diff --name-only a779ade8 c1452fd1`). Every source and test byte equals the gated head, so my source review of a779ade8 carries over.\n- **Source gate.** `gate.txt` (SHA-256 `4c7c6b88…`) names head a779ade8, tree 37e8a416, changed files 0, and ends \"gate passed\", exit 0, 990.83 s. Node 246, Counting 60, Plain 5,089 with one skipped, Native 1,239 with two skipped, crossings 0 lost, 4 stale, 0 unowned. Scale was omitted because no changed path selects it. The counts match END a7e42f58.\n- **Notes-only gate.** `gate.txt` (SHA-256 `5ed24069…`) names head c1452fd1, tree df2b7db7, ends \"gate passed\", exit 0, 31.69 s, and records \"test skipped: only paths under notes/ changed\". It matches END a48d73a0.\n- **Hashes.** All 8 distinct SHA-256 values in the new implementation note match files in the retained evidence directory, including the control log (`b4ed9dfa…`), the interrupted two-lane gate (`99ad3c00…`) and the source gate.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main (8a9f9d1e) is clean with tree df2b7db7. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 5 commits, `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `git diff --check` is clean. The added lines carry no other project's name and no `/Users/` path.\n- **Control.** The log shows 3 passed and 1 failed with the fail effect resetting the count: \"fulfill → fail: expected +0 to be 1\" at `commitments.test.ts:188`, the assertion line at the head. `apps/counter` has no diff between 95ec0456 and 8a9f9d1e, so the control's source basis holds. The log carries the test's earlier title, and the implementation note says so.\n\n## Wake rate\nThe group adds no alarm, retry or reschedule. The wake floor and requests per room per hour are unchanged. Nothing deploys: the change is a client library, test, documentation and note change, with no Worker, Durable Object or schema source.\n\n## XD-1 draft revision fence\n- **Architecture.** `draftRevision` is the digest of the canonical stored draft, exposed as `revision` on every draft view. `submit(slot, now, revision)` checks it in the first member fence, after `taken` and before `state`, the `now` check and any signing. The second fence already requires the same stored draft (`same(again.current, stored)`), so a draft that changes after the first check stops with `state` and nothing signs. A malformed revision stops with `shape` before any await. `DraftStop` gains `draft-changed`. The two-argument form is unchanged, and both the package guide and the scope-client note say so.\n- **Security.** A member can no longer sign content another tab replaced under the same key, provided the caller passes the revision. The revision is a digest of values the view already shows, so it discloses nothing new. The new test counts `signs()` and copies: the stale call signs nothing, and the fresh revision signs once. The revision changes on any stored change, including a return. That is intended: the member reads the new view.\n- **Simplification.** One helper, one optional argument, one stop value. The guide names `revision` and `draft-changed` and tells the application to show the updated draft.\n- **Witness.** A red test under real custody with two clients on one store. The paired control submits the new revision and signs.\n\n## Counting finite fulfillment pairs\n- **Architecture.** One pure test enumerates all 16 ordered pairs of fulfill, fail, cancel and expire at target 3, so both steps stay under the target. It compares `lastNumber` with a count tracked in the test, not with the production fold. Each step drives the real validator, judges and drain.\n- **Security.** Test only. The fixture gives each actor every grant, so the test checks the count while the signer guards stay in place. The note says so.\n- **Simplification.** No generator or shrinking library. The README counts (five tests) and file list agree with the test file.\n- **Witness.** The fault control distinguishes: `fulfill → fail` reads 0 against an expected 1 with the fail effect reset, and the pin check is deselected because the control changes the definition bytes. The note states that the native Counting witness was read, not run.\n\n## Security cleanup\n- **Architecture.** Three small changes. The entry-points document now says that distinct /48s can still fill the creation table and that further identities share the bounded overflow window (my non-blocking item 1 on the stack review). The S7 note drops the incoming-power sentence (item 4). The real-bin CLI case runs `new` and `check` in sequence through one `spawnSync` helper and keeps its 30 s deadline (item 3).\n- **Security.** No source change. The document sentence is accurate against the /48 arithmetic.\n- **Simplification.** The removed `execFile` and `allSettled` overlap saves lines and a second spawn environment. The case passed in the gate.\n\n## Notes read at the head\n- `notes/2026-11-21-property-based-testing.md`: the Status line now says the gate passed on a779ade8 (END